  "id": "COMPOUND:30453 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Yuanhunine appears to have a complex relationship with DNA polymerase iota, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that ultimately direct their activity to this enzyme. The evidence suggests that Yuanhunine indirectly influences DNA polymerase iota through its interaction with Thioredoxin, a protein involved in mitochondrial processes. This pathway is further supported by the fact that Thioredoxin, mitochondrial is targeted by three distinct compounds—[1-(4,8-Dimethoxy-1-methyl-2-oxoquinolin-3-yl)-3-methylbut-3-en-2-yl] hexadecanoate, Anguidine deriv scirpentriol, and Nectriapyrone—all of which are linked to DNA polymerase iota. While the exact mechanism by which these compounds interact with Thioredoxin and subsequently affect DNA polymerase iota remains unclear, the integrated evidence points to a potential role for Thioredoxin in mediating this relationship. The presence of multiple pathways converging on DNA polymerase iota underscores the complexity of the interaction network, but the core mechanism appears to involve the targeting of Thioredoxin, which in turn influences the activity of DNA polymerase iota.",
